Title: FUN'S Cross-Word Puzzle
Author: Elizabeth M. Rutzinger
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-05-10
Number: 21
Notes: A 19-wide diamond with a diamond-shaped hole in the centre (r6 c10 widening to r10 c6-c14 and narrowing to r14 c10; shown as _), so the middle column holds two short words (53-54 TULLE above the hole, 55-56 ILIAD below). Number printed in the heading ("FUN'S CROSS-WORD PUZZLE No. 21"). Credit as printed in the intro: "Miss Elizabeth M. Rutzinger, who sent in the ingeniously constructed cross word puzzle published in last week's FUN, has contributed another." Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_05_10_89.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_05_17_89.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.



