1-2. A conveyance. ~ BUS
3-4. An alluvial deposit, formed at the mouth of a river. ~ DELTA
5-6. Those who heal. ~ HEALERS
7-8. It has thirty days. ~ SEPTEMBER
9-10. A confused condition. ~ CHAOS
11-12. A sewing machine. ~ SOWER
13-14. A judicial tribunal. ~ COURT
15-16. A frolic. ~ REVEL
17-18. Sailors. ~ SALTS
19-20. What the sun does. ~ RISES
21-22. Luminous circles. ~ HALOS
23-24. Before 9 o'clock. ~ EIGHT
25-26. A small wild animal. ~ TAPIR
27-28. Where milk is converted into butter and cheese. ~ DAIRY
29-30. A subject of discourse. ~ TOPIC
31-32. To tarnish. ~ SULLY
33-34. To hand over for consideration. ~ REFER
35-36. Incrusted with scales. ~ SCALY
37-38. A large sea duck. ~ EIDER
39-40. Inclined to take fright. ~ SCARY
41-42. The chocolate tree. ~ CACAO
43-44. An anecdote. ~ STORY
45-46. To tint with red. ~ RUBRICATE
47-48. Flat narrow partitions. ~ RIGLETS
49-50. A deteriorating quality. ~ TAINT
51-52. A genii worshiped in Burma. ~ NAT
53-54. Used for veils and light dresses. ~ TULLE
55-56. A Greek epic poem. ~ ILIAD
1-10. What your heart does. ~ BEATS
3-14. A railroad station. ~ DEPOT
5-18. Listens. ~ HEARS
7-22. Closes. ~ SHUTS
9-41. Capable of producing color. ~ COLORIFIC
13-37. The part of a turtle next the lower shell. ~ CALIPEE
17-33. Qpality affecting the sense of taste. ~ SAPOR
21-29. A covering for the head. ~ HAT
30-45. A fragrant tree. ~ CEDAR
34-47. To happen again. ~ RECUR
38-49. A wooden drinking vessel. ~ RABIT
42-51. A musical instrument. ~ ORGAN
2-11. Stalks. ~ STEMS
4-15. A bower, or summer house. ~ ARBOR
6-19. A drain. ~ SEWER
8-23. To surpass. ~ REVIE
12-44. Pertaining to a remainder. ~ RESIDUARY
16-40. Lawfully. ~ LEGALLY
20-36. Shyly. ~ SHILY
24-32. To attempt. ~ TRY
31-46. A fright. ~ SCARE
35-48. Natives of Scotland. ~ SCOTS
39-50. German for dwelling place. ~ STATT
43-52. Perfume. ~ SCENT



